==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~30 seconds<sup>300f~900f</sup>.
*1 [[Madam Peng]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*2 [[Malizabeth]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
*4 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] spawns as the boss after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The Angelic Sleipnir is the biggest threat here, as their high attack rate makes the use of low-range units like [[Barista Cat (Special Cat)|Silver Nyanko Ranger]] somewhat difficult. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist Cat]] is a fantastic meatshield here to ward off Sleipnir, especially alongside a cheap meatshield like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]]. [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] works as a substitute in case you don't own Artist Cat. As for your attackers, you should bring units with high range like [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Legs Cat]]/[[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]], etc. Dark Emperor Nyandam simply serves to occasionally kill off your melee units up front. The peons can be taken care of with other Nyanko Rangers like [[Scarf Cat (Special Cat)|Red Nyanko Ranger]] and [[Fedora Cat (Special Cat)|Blue Nyanko Ranger]].

If you own [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] by this point,  you can actually rush down Nyandam as soon as he spawns by sending Bahamut out first thing. This is especially useful for fast clears, as it makes dealing with Angelic Sleipnir a breeze.

